  "from": "2015",
  "description": "Fuselage: Missouri flag horizontally: red crown, white middle through the window line, blue belly; the Missouri coat of arms (two brown grizzly bears holding a shield, 'UNITED WE STAND' banner, gold helmet) on the forward fuselage over the windows inside a blue ring of white stars. Cheatlines: Red/white/blue horizontal bands running full length. Tail: Heart fin with white 'Southwest'. Engines: Cowlings carry the state seal quarters (blue with crescent moon, red with bear, US eagle) (approximate). Winglets: approximate. Titles: 'Southwest' white on lower fin; 'Missouri One' small by cockpit. Artwork: Missouri coat of arms. Colors hex: approximate.",
